  "routeAdjustment": "Reuse existing all-level monic relations to derive integrality instead of introducing a degree-based finiteness premise. Reuse the native simple-extension construction through the already proved local embedding theorem. Use Subfield.inclusion for literal identity transport to avoid rational scalar-instance diamonds. Native multiset divisibility shortens the product comparison. The actual bidirectional prime product removes any symmetry premise.",
  "discharged": "Existing all-divisor monic relations directly prove integrality and monicity of the original expanded minimal polynomial. Native multiset divisibility reduces its product identity to individual indexed roots and the exact simple-field degree. Existing simple-extension embeddings transport a lower-level root to the actual original full field under explicit lower-level generation. The full degree-p+1 step identifies the prime relation with the relative minimal polynomial. The degree-p step removes the known preceding j root and proves every specified distinct twisted branch is a relative root. Native tower divisibility transfers these roots to the original base minimal polynomial.",
  "remaining": "The degree/generation induction must supply the lower-level generation and step-degree inputs, and prove the specified branch differs from the removed preceding root. Full indexed-root construction, composite generation and degree, modular ramification and numerical genus remain required, followed by analytic realization and the period/arithmetic/symmetric-power gates. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20.",
